t status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>IKEHATA TAKASHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SUZUKI YASUO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TOKYO ELECTRONICS</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>IKEHATA, TAKASHI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SUZUKI, YASUO</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TOKYO DENSHI KABUSHIKI KAISHA</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>IKEHATA TAKASHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SUZUKI YASUO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>IKEHATA, TAKASHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SUZUKI, YASUO</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>Laser light is reflected by opposed concave mirrors a plurality of times so that the paths of reflection may converge to form a reaction space of high photon density. Any of reactive objects such as gas, liquid, solid, plasma, particle beam and electron beam can be introduced into the reaction space for photoreaction with the laser light to induce optical pumping, photoionization, photolysis, photodecomposition, photosynthesis, photometric analysis, etc.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>D'après cette invention, une lumière laser est réfléchie plusieurs fois par des miroirs concaves opposés de sorte que les trajets de réflexion convergent et forment un espace de réaction d'une grande densité photonique. Des objets réactifs quels qu'ils soient, tels qu'un gaz, un liquide, un plasma, un solide, un faisceau de particules ou un faisceau d'électrons, peuvent être introduits dans l'espace de réaction en vue d'une photoréaction avec la lumière laser de manière à induire un pompage optique, une photo-ionisation, une photolyse, une photodécomposition, une photosynthèse, une analyse photométrique, etc.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>